M38a TMS99000 semantic p-code map
=================================

This is the review authority for the active CC_CG99 backend. Every entry
states the required result, not merely a mnemonic substitution. Generated sequences use SP, never R10.

Register contract
-----------------
R4  primary accumulator and C return value
R3  secondary / left operand
R5  argument count / helper input
FP  frame pointer (FP EQU 9)
SP  software stack pointer (SP EQU 10)
R11 BL link register
R0-R2 backend/runtime scratch

Helper contract
---------------
Runtime helpers use the native Small-C/call.A99 convention: R3 is the
secondary/left operand and R4 is the primary/right operand.  Helpers may
destroy R0-R5 and R11, preserve R6-R10 and R12-R15, and return a word result
in R4.  _ccdiv returns quotient in R4 and remainder in R3.

Unsigned arithmetic note: signed DIV/MOD use _ccdiv, but DIV12u/MOD12u use
the native unsigned TMS9900 DIV instruction. Unsigned right shift has its own
LSR12 p-code and lowers through the existing _ccusr helper; ASR12 remains signed.

ID  NAME      CLASS    TMS99000 SEMANTICS / INITIAL LOWERING
--  --------  -------  -------------------------------------------------------
01  ADD12     DIRECT   A R3,R4                         ;R4 = R4 + R3
02  ADDSP     DIRECT   AI SP,<n>                       ;omit when n == 0
03  AND12     DIRECT   INV R3 / SZC R3,R4             ;R4 &= old R3
04  ANEG1     DIRECT   NEG R4                          ;arithmetic negate primary
05  ARGCNTn   DIRECT   LI R5,<n>, or CLR R5 for zero
06  ASL12     HELPER   BL @_ccasl##                    ;R3 << R4 -> R4
07  ASR12     HELPER   BL @_ccasr##                    ;signed R3 >> R4 -> R4
08  CALL1     DIRECT   CALL *R4                        ;indirect function call
09  CALLm     DIRECT   CALL @<m>                       ;direct function call
10  BYTE_     EMITTER  BYTE                            ;start byte list
11  BYTEn     EMITTER  BYTE <n>
12  BYTEr0    EMITTER  zero-fill <n> bytes
13  COM1      DIRECT   INV R4                          ;ones complement primary
14  DBL1      DIRECT   A R4,R4                         ;primary *= 2
15  DBL2      DIRECT   A R3,R3                         ;secondary *= 2
16  DIV12     HELPER   BL @_ccdiv##                    ;R3 / R4 -> quotient R4
17  DIV12u    DIRECT   R3/R4 via native DIV             ;unsigned quotient -> R4
18  ENTER     DIRECT   STWP WP / DECT SP / MOV FP,*SP / MOV SP,FP
19  EQ10f     CONTROL  jump <n> when R4 != 0
20  EQ12      HELPER   BL @_cceq##                     ;R3 == R4 -> R4 0/1
21  GE10f     CONTROL  jump <n> when signed R4 < 0
22  GE12      HELPER   BL @_ccge##                     ;R3 >= R4
23  GE12u     HELPER   BL @_ccuge##                    ;unsigned R3 >= R4
24  POINT1l   DIRECT   LI R4,_<l>+<n>                  ;literal address
25  POINT1m   DIRECT   LI R4,<m>                       ;symbol address
26  GETb1m    DIRECT   MOVB @<m>,R4 / SRA R4,8         ;signed global byte
27  GETb1mu   DIRECT   MOVB @<m>,R4 / SRL R4,8         ;unsigned global byte
28  GETb1p    DIRECT   MOVB @<n>(R3),R4 / SRA R4,8     ;signed pointer byte
29  GETb1pu   DIRECT   MOVB @<n>(R3),R4 / SRL R4,8     ;unsigned pointer byte
30  GETw1m    DIRECT   MOV @<m>,R4                     ;global word
31  GETw1n    DIRECT   LI R4,<n>, or CLR R4 for zero
32  GETw1p    DIRECT   MOV @<n>(R3),R4                 ;pointer word
33  GETw2n    DIRECT   LI R3,<n>, or CLR R3 for zero
34  GT10f     CONTROL  jump <n> when signed R4 <= 0
35  GT12      HELPER   BL @_ccgt##                     ;R3 > R4
36  GT12u     HELPER   BL @_ccugt##                    ;unsigned R3 > R4
37  WORD_     EMITTER  WORD                            ;start word list
38  WORDn     EMITTER  WORD <n>
39  WORDr0    EMITTER  zero-fill <n> words
40  JMPm      CONTROL  B @_<n>
41  LABm      EMITTER  _<n>:
42  LE10f     CONTROL  jump <n> when signed R4 > 0
43  LE12      HELPER   BL @_ccle##                     ;R3 <= R4
44  LE12u     HELPER   BL @_ccule##                    ;unsigned R3 <= R4
45  LNEG1     HELPER   BL @_cclneg##                   ;!R4 -> R4 0/1
46  LT10f     CONTROL  jump <n> when signed R4 >= 0
47  LT12      HELPER   BL @_cclt##                     ;R3 < R4
48  LT12u     HELPER   BL @_ccult##                    ;unsigned R3 < R4
49  MOD12     HELPER   BL @_ccdiv## / SWAP12           ;remainder -> R4
50  MOD12u    DIRECT   R3%R4 via native DIV             ;unsigned remainder -> R4
51  MOVE21    DIRECT   MOV R4,R3                       ;primary -> secondary
52  MUL12     HELPER   BL @_ccmult##                   ;R3 * R4 -> R4
53  MUL12u    HELPER   BL @_ccmult##                   ;same historical helper
54  NE10f     CONTROL  jump <n> when R4 == 0
55  NE12      HELPER   BL @_ccne##                     ;R3 != R4 -> R4 0/1
56  NEARm     EMITTER  WORD _<n>                       ;switch target address
57  OR12      DIRECT   SOC R3,R4                       ;R4 |= R3
58  POINT1s   DIRECT   MOV FP,R4 / AI R4,<n>           ;local address
59  POP2      DIRECT   MOV *SP+,R3                     ;pop secondary
60  PUSH1     DIRECT   DECT SP / MOV R4,*SP            ;push primary
61  PUTbm1    DIRECT   MOVB @2*R4+1(WP),@<m>           ;primary low byte
62  PUTbp1    DIRECT   MOVB @2*R4+1(WP),*R3            ;through secondary ptr
63  PUTwm1    DIRECT   MOV R4,@<m>
64  PUTwp1    DIRECT   MOV R4,*R3
65  rDEC1     DIRECT   DEC R4
66  REFm      EMITTER  _<n>                            ;symbol in data list
67  RETURN    DIRECT   MOV FP,SP / MOV *SP+,FP / RET
68  rINC1     DIRECT   INC R4
69  SUB12     DIRECT   S R4,R3 / MOV R3,R4             ;R4 = left - right
70  SWAP12    DIRECT   MOV R3,R0 / MOV R4,R3 / MOV R0,R4
71  SWAP1s    DIRECT   MOV *SP,R0 / MOV R4,*SP / MOV R0,R4
72  SWITCH    HELPER   CALL @_ccswitc##                ;XOP6 return points at inline switch table
73  XOR12     DIRECT   XOR R3,R4
74  LSR12     HELPER   BL @_ccusr##                    ;unsigned R3 >> R4 -> R4

Notes requiring hardware/toolchain proof
----------------------------------------
1. BYTEr0/WORDr0 must explicitly produce zero storage. BSS is acceptable only
   after the R99 linker/load path is proved to initialise it to zero.
2. Conditional p-codes 19/21/34/42/46/54 need generated local skip labels;
   their conditions above are copied from the blessed 8086 template semantics.
3. Variable shifts use call.A99 helpers. ASR12 selects _ccasr and LSR12 selects
   _ccusr; both explicitly preserve a zero shift count.
4. PUTbm1/PUTbp1 preserve primary R4 by reading its low byte directly from
   workspace memory at @2*R4+1(WP). ENTER executes STWP WP so WP is valid.
5. POINT1s forms an address in primary R4. MOV @<n>(FP),R4 would load the local
   value and is therefore not equivalent.
